      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Multivessel diffuse coronary arteriopathy is the hallmark of chronic diabetic patients. The ideal method of revascularising this group of patients is controversial. This review examines the various modalities available in the revascularisation of coronary artery disease in diabetic patients. Various trials have been conducted to compare the effectiveness of surgical and percutaneous methods of revascularisation. Most of the important trials like BARI, CABRI, EMORY and Duke's database are critically analysed and a meaningful practical strategy to manage this difficult subgroup of patients is outlined. The recommendations may change after a few years if the new coated stents prove their worth."},
